James inquired about encountering an "undefined control sequence" error related to the LaTeX code `$\gt$`. I clarified that `\gt` is not a standard command in LaTeX for the greater-than symbol, advising him to use the `>` character directly in math mode instead. Key points included potential issues like incorrect usage, font or package conflicts, and peculiar behaviors in certain TeX distributions. I provided an example using `amsmath` to illustrate proper syntax for the greater-than symbol. I also encouraged him to share more context if the problem persisted.
